{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Please pardon.</b> Since we find that He said, “if they see the land” after “I have forgiven according to your word,” we know that the word סלח נא is an extension of anger, and likewise ונסלח לו, until he does complete repentance." "<b>As the greatness of Your kindness.</b> On account of Your great kindness." "<b>And as You have borne.</b> Like the meaning of נושא עון (bearing iniquity)." "<b>And until now.</b> Until this place, or from the day they went out of Egypt until this day. For sometimes הנה is a place name, as in “they came here tonight,” and sometimes it is a sign of time, as in “and I have not seen him until now,” and I have already explained this."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:39.037889535Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}